        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can add a background image to all content pages in your document by setting the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-background-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " document attribute. You can also set the background images for recto and verso pages separately using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-background-image-recto"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " and "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-background-image-verso"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " document attributes. You can set (or override) the background image applied to the title page using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "title-page-background-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " document attribute. If you want to overlay a background image on top of the page content (i.e., a watermark), you can do so using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-foreground-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "This page explains how these document attributes are used. It also covers how attributes on the image macro can be used to control the size, fit, and position of the image. All the document attributes covered on this page must be defined in the document header."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As an alternative to using document attributes, you can define these background images and the foreground image "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "in your theme"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "theme:images.html"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
        "context": "preamble",
        "id": null,
        "outline": null,
        "roles": [],
        "title": null
      },
      {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Background images can be applied to all content pages using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-background-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " document attribute. A content page is defined as every page in the document except for cover and imported pages. The list of content pages includes the title page as well as non-facing pages in a prepress document."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "admonition",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "As a counterpart, a foreground image can be added to all pages using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-foreground-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ". Unlike the background image, the foreground image cannot be added per side or page layout."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null,
            "type": "note"
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "The "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-background-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attribute accepts an inline image macro. The target of the image macro can be "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "an absolute path or a path relative to imagesdir"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "image-paths-and-formats.html#imagesdir"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Document Title\n:page-background-image: image:bg.png[]"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "You can also assign a page background image "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "per side"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#recto-verso"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " or "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "per page layout"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#page-layout"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "When you set "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "page-background-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", the specified image will be applied to the title page as well. You can specify a different image for the title page using the "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "title-page-background-image"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " document attribute."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Document Title\n:doctype: book\n:page-background-image: image:bg.png[]\n:title-page-background-image: image:title-bg.png[]"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "Alternately, you can turn off the background image on the title page by assigning the value "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "none"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "listing",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "= Document Title\n:doctype: book\n:page-background-image: image:bg.png[]\n:title-page-background-image: none"
              }
            ],
            "language": "asciidoc",
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          },
          {
            "context": "paragraph",
            "id": null,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "By default, page background images are automatically scaled to fit the bounds of the page (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fit=contain"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ") and centered (i.e., "
              },
              {
                "id": null,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "position=center"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "monospace",
                "roles": []
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": "). To alter this behavior, you can set the "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "fit"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#fit"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": ", sizing, and "
              },
              {
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "kind": "text",
                    "value": "position"
                  }
                ],
                "kind": "xref",
                "target": "#position"
              },
              {
                "kind": "text",
                "value": " attributes on the image macro."
              }
            ],
            "roles": [],
            "title": null
          }
        ],
